      ]
    },
    "partial_duplicate_rule": "Within each row, the last populated natural column carrying a repeated label wins. If that later duplicate column is absent in a partial final row, an earlier occurrence survives there; the selected natural column can therefore differ in the final row."
  },
  "limits": [
    "No claim that Rev7 used a malformed key or this tool.",
    "A malformed-key ciphertext may be shorter than its pre-AMSCO input; deleted bytes cannot be inferred by inverse permutation alone.",
    "Per-character trim removes space, TAB, LF, VT, CR, and NUL before matrix construction; for already whitespace-free uppercase hexadecimal this does not change bytes.",
    "No PHP runtime was available; the harness models the cited assignment/read loops and historical scalar/null behavior directly. No target ciphertext was read or evaluated."
  ],
